My human ranger was searching the mines for some interesting stuff (she
already found a luckstone in the main dungeon)... I was nervous of the
polymorph traps because a) I didn't have MR and b) I didn't want some
Arch Lich show up.

The main problem was that I didn't have any blindfold or towel. There
just hadn't been any. And almost all the mine levels were dark (even
the shop level). So there wasn't any way to check the monster
situation. Though I had the confidence to proceed with AC -6,
reflecton, being fast and wielding +0 Grimtooth.

Then I faced some invisible monster. "It hits. It hits. It hits. You
hear a mumbled curse." I hit it two times and it dies. I never
suspected it to be anything tougher than a gnomish wizard. When I saw
the corpse I was terrified. It had been a titan! All the possible nasty
tricks he could have pulled spring in my mind. Hordes of nasties,
destroy armour and possibly even touch of death (?!?).

Why didn't he do anything? Was I just lucky or are polymorphed monsters
weaker than the "real" monsters? I definitely felt lucky after that
incident! So when I got to the Mine's end and an invisible monster made
me stunned I panicked and quaffed a potion of blindness to see if it
was another titan. But this time it was a gnomish wizard. :)



